    "summary": "Cloth, woman&#039;s wrapper, made of natural-coloured hand-spun cotton composed of ten plain woven narrow strips, all of which have bands of openwork formed by tying warp and weft threads together. One strip has two horizontal beige stripes. The strips are joined together along the central sections (but not at the ends) by means of decorative braiding; the top two strips re an exception and have been sewn together. The strip at the top has an extension to form a tuck-in tie fastener. The ends of wrapper have been left as a fringe.",
